# Initial Class Diagram Analysis

The initial classes identified for the Student Activities Management System (SAMS) are:

- User
- Student
- Organizer
- Student Affairs Staff
- Activity
- Registration
- Attendance
- Notification
- Certificate
- Waiting List

These classes represent the main users and functions of the system.

The Student can browse activities, register for activities, receive notifications, record attendance, and obtain certificates.

The Organizer can create and manage activities, review registrations, and monitor attendance.

The Student Affairs Staff can supervise activities, review reports, and manage the overall system.

More attributes, methods, and relationships will be defined in the next project phase.

---

# Initial Relational Database Analysis

The initial database tables identified for the system are:

- Users
- Students
- Organizers
- Student_Affairs_Staff
- Activities
- Registrations
- Attendance
- Notifications
- Certificates
- Waiting_List

Each table will contain a primary key.

Foreign keys will connect related tables. For example:

- Student_ID → Registrations
- Activity_ID → Registrations
- Activity_ID → Attendance
- User_ID → Notifications
- Registration_ID → Certificates

The complete database schema, including attributes, primary keys, foreign keys, and relationships, will be finalized in the next phase.
